

Count the distinct number of patients who have controlled blood pressure from the temp table of valid bloodpressures "validbp" we are only joining those with encounters from the encounters table
and grouping by the controlled column, which presents either a yes or no.  

select bp.controlled, count(distinct e.patientid) 'Number of Patients'
from ##validbp bp
join encounters e on bp.encounterid=e.EncounterID
group by bp.controlled

How many individual patients have had an elevated bloodpressure AND a controlled bloodpressure 

select count(distinct e.patientid)'Patients'
from ##validbp
join encounters e on bp.encounterid= e.encounterid 
where bp.controlled= 'N' 
and e.patientid in (select patientid from encounters e join ##validbp bp on
e.encounterid=bp.encounterid where bp.controlled='Y')


What is the most often prescribed medication

select MedName, count(PatientID)'Number of Patients'
from Medications
group by MedName
order by count(PatientID) desc

What are the top 3 most often prescribed medication?

select top 3 medname, count(distinct patientid)
from Medications
group by medname 
order by count(distinct patientid)desc



Return the facility and number of visits at that facility where the blood pressure was not elevated. Order the output from highest to lowest visit counts 

select f.name 'Facility Name', count(e.encounterid) 'Number of Visits'
from encounters e
join facilities f on f.facilityid = e.facilityid
join ##validbp bp on bp.encounterid = e.encounterid
where bp.controlled = 'Y'
group by f.name
order by count(e.encounterid) desc




Return PatientID, Patient Name(LastName, Firstname in one column), and the number of diagnoses each patient has. Order by highest to lowest diagnosis count 

select p.patientid, p.lastname+ ', ' + p.firstname 'Patient Name', count(d.ICDCode)'Number of Diagnoses'
from diagnoses d 
join patients p on p.patientid= d.patientid 
group by p.patientid, p.lastname+ ', ' +p.firstname
order by count(d.ICDCode) desc

Return number of patients with controlled BP by provider specialty 

select count(distinct e.patientid)'Number of Patients', d.specialty'Doctor Specialty'
from encounters e
join doctors d on d.doctorid= e.doctorid
join ##validbp bp on bp.encounterid = e.encounterid
where bp.controlled = 'Y'
group by d.specialty
order by count(distinct e.patientid) desc


